  },
  "summary": "Working hours cannot be opened for a staff member who belongs to another location",
  "description": {
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1,
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Description"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "A staff member's working hours cannot be opened at all if that person belongs to a different location from the one you are currently working in. The Staff list shows everyone in the organisation, so you can find the person, open them, and switch on "
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Set custom hours for this technician",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": " \u2014 and at that point the screen gives up with an error and switches the toggle back off. There is no way to reach their hours from the location you are in."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "It matters because the Schedule uses each technician's working hours for the start time of a new shift, for the before-hours and after-hours conflict warnings and for the capacity bars. A shop that runs two locations cannot set those hours for anyone outside whichever location they happen to be viewing, and the screen gives no hint that switching location is what is needed \u2014 it simply looks broken."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "This affects a substantial part of the staff list rather than one unlucky record: of the 161 people in the list, 63 cannot have their hours opened from the Heavy Duty location and 98 can."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "heading",
     "attrs": {
      "level": 3
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Branch / Environment"
